  <h2 id="ai-layer">Where AI changes the plan</h2>

  <p>
    AI now touches every blocker, but in a different way. Ask a practical question first: which part of my
    current work has become easier, and which part still needs me?
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>No shortlists:</strong> AI can speed up building a first sample, but you still need to explain what you built and how you checked it. "Used AI" is not proof. "Used AI to draft, checked the numbers, and fixed three errors" is.</li>
    <li><strong>No offers:</strong> use AI to practise mock questions, then record yourself answering in your own words.</li>
    <li><strong>No growth:</strong> automate one repeat task at work, and measure the time saved. That is a visible scope win.</li>
    <li><strong>Pay capped:</strong> domain knowledge plus AI workflow design is one of the stronger multipliers, but only if you can verify outputs and protect private data.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      AI raises the value of people who can judge output, and lowers the value of people who only
      repeat tasks. It does not promise a raise or job security on its own. The result depends on the
      problem you point it at and whether someone can see the outcome.
    </p>
  </div>

